  "scope": [
    "Module UART as delivered by ST (STM32CubeN6 v1.4.0), FROZEN: the UART HAL component (classic, handle-based) and the USART LL component (header-only inline functions) under one functional-level requirement set. The delivered HAL does not use the delivered LL: the two components are parallel public APIs over the same peripheral.",
    "In scope (HAL): initialisation and de-initialisation with their platform hooks; configuration through the initialisation structure (baud rate, word length, stop bits, parity, direction, oversampling); FIFO mode and FIFO thresholds; blocking transmit and receive; interrupt-driven transmit, receive and interrupt handling; DMA-driven transmit and receive; abort of transmit, receive or both, blocking and interrupt-driven; callback registration and unregistration and the transmit/receive complete, half-complete, error and abort-complete callbacks; state and error queries.",
    "In scope (LL): enable and disable; configuration of the asynchronous mode (direction, parity, data width, stop bits, oversampling, prescaler, baud rate); FIFO; DMA request enable; transmit, receive and error interrupt enable and status with the corresponding flags and flag clears; data transmit and receive.",
    "Out of scope (delivered; listed by the governance inventory): half-duplex, LIN, multiprocessor, RS-485, receive-to-idle and its event callbacks, receiver timeout, DMA pause/resume/stop, stop-mode wake-up, the FIFO event callbacks and the vendor-internal helper functions of the HAL; LIN, smartcard, IrDA, auto baud rate, wake-up, RS-485 driver enable, synchronous and SPI-slave mode, hardware flow control and the advanced pin and data options of the LL.",
    "SWE.1 only, at the functional level: register-level detail and concrete negative cases belong to SWE.3."
  ],
